JSX-Javascript Xml
It is a syntax extension for JavaScript primarily used in React to describe what the user interface (UI) should look like.
It allows developers to write HTML-like structures directly inside JavaScript files.

How it Works
Browsers cannot read JSX directly. Under the hood, a tool like Babel compiles the JSX code down into regular JavaScript function calls (React.createElement()), which then generate the objects that build the webpage

